  "description": "Active Directory health for AD1 and AD2, with interpretation guidance, Windows metrics from Prometheus, and Event Viewer logs from Loki.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "liveNow": false,
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "description": "Quick interpretation guide for the Active Directory health panels.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Active Directory health guide\nEach panel has an **info icon** beside its title with metric-specific good, warning, and bad guidance. Green generally means healthy; yellow means watch or investigate if sustained; red means action is recommended. Metrics without universal thresholds should be compared between AD1 and AD2 and against their normal baseline. **No data is not always healthy**—check Telemetry age first to confirm both controllers are reporting."
      }
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "max": 300,
          "min": 0,
          "noValue": "No telemetry",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 45
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 90
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.6.1",
      "targets": [
        {
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max by (host) (time() - timestamp(windows_os_info{host=~\"$host\"}))",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{host}}",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Telemetry age",
      "type": "stat",
      "description": "How recently each domain controller delivered metrics. Good: under 45 seconds. Warning: 45-90 seconds. Bad: over 90 seconds or no telemetry. Stale data usually means Alloy stopped, the host is unreachable, or remote-write delivery is failing."
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "max": 6,
          "min": 0,
          "noValue": "No data",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 5
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 6
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 4
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
